q=dict(question='After a candidate starts a second real campaign, can delayed genuine grant responses from its first campaign contribute to leadership before a majority of current-term grants has been delivered?',importance='Counting old-term grants as support for a new campaign would break local authority qualification. The direct question is current-term election support, not a demonstrated conflicting leader or client decision.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',participants=['Candidate RawNode','Two voting peers','FIFO local storage workers and transport scheduler'],objects=['Actual first and second campaign vote requests/responses','Persistent HardState term/vote','Current campaign vote map','Public leader role and term'],contexts=['Three fixed bootstrapped voters, AsyncStorageWrites, PreVote disabled','Two explicit Campaign calls before any first-campaign grant is delivered to the candidate','First and second campaign responses retain original message identity and term'],event_paths=['Campaign term 2 -> actual peer grants/self grant packaged after storage; transport holds responses','Campaign term 3 -> reset votes and emit actual new requests; independently hold new grants','Release actual term-2 grants, then current self grant and one remote term-3 grant; observe BasicStatus after each fixed phase'],activity_classes=['A2','A6','A1'],behavior_ids=['B_elect_transfer','B_role_reset'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_step_context_and_storage':'Filters stale terms before candidate response tally.','B_append_response_packaging':'Publishes real and self vote responses only after local storage work.','B_configuration':'Bootstrap establishes the fixed electorate.'},fact_ids=[fid],obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Step returns on lower-term ordinary responses, so old VoteResp should never reach poll.','becomeCandidate resets Votes and increments term.','stepCandidate independently rejects pre-vote response type during real candidacy.'],unknowns=['Construct both campaigns and delayed grants through actual storage and network producers without injecting vote messages.','Fix an independent delivered-grant ledger by sender and original term, and observe leadership transitions under a bounded schedule.'],trigger_rationale='The sender map carries no term tag, so freshness depends on the preceding gate and reset. Consecutive campaigns with delayed genuine responses test this concrete dependency; current self-plus-peer grants supply a permitted control. This avoids the unresolved snapshot/configuration caller contract.')
